0061 \"CALOHA:TS-1164\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000061 \"FMA:63002\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000061 \"cementum secreting cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D010006\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000062 \"Skeletogenic cell that secretes osteoid, is capable of producing mineralized (hydroxyapatite) matrix, is located adjacent to or within osteoid tissue, and arises from the transformation of a preosteoblast cell.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000062 \"BTO:0001593\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000062 \"CALOHA:TS-0720\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000062 \"FMA:66780\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FB:ma\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000063 \"OBSOLETE: A classification of cells by their microscopic appearance.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:consider obo:CL_0000063 \"CL:0000000\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:consider obo:CL_0000063 \"CL:0000003\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:consider obo:CL_0000063 \"CL:0001034\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000064 \"A cell that has a filiform extrusion of the cell surface.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000064 \"VHOG:0001532\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000064 \"XAO:0000031\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34335193\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37008045\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9550134\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.3389/fncel.2021.703951\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.britannica.com/science/ependymal-cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000065 \"A neuroepithelial glial cell, derived from a radial glial cell originating from the neuroectoderm, lines the ventricles of the brain and the central canal of the spinal cord. This cell is characterized by the presence of cilia on its apical surface, which can be motile or non-motile.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000065 \"BTO:0001724\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000065 \"FMA:70550\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.53347/rID-51713\") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_0000065 \"ependymocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FB:ma\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D004847\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000066 \"A cell that is usually found in a two-dimensional sheet with a free surface. The cell has a cytoskeleton that allows for tight cell to cell contact and for cell polarity where apical part is directed towards the lumen and the basal part to the basal lamina.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000066 \"BTO:0000414\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000066 \"CALOHA:TS-2026\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000066 \"CARO:0000077\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000066 \"FMA:66768\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000066 \"WBbt:0003672\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000066 \"epitheliocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000067 \"An epithelial cell that has a cilia.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000067 \"FMA:70605\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000068 \"An epithelial cell that is part of a duct.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000071 \"An endothelial cell that lines the vasculature.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12662305\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000074 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0000066 from Plant Ontology instead. A cell that constitutes the mesophyll of a hydathode and is located between the xylem endings and the epidermis. Proposed to be involved in the retrieval of solutes from the xylem sap.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO:0002065\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000075 \"A columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell is a cell usually found in a two dimensional sheet with a free surface. Columnar/cuboidal epithelial cells take on the shape of a column or cube.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000076 \"CALOHA:TS-1249\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26106328\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000077 \"A flat, squamous-like epithelial cell of mesodermal origin. It forms the mesothelium, which lines the body's serous cavities including the pleural, peritoneal, and pericardial spaces. This cell plays a crucial role in synthesizing and secreting lubricants, such as glycosaminoglycans and surfactants, which minimize friction between adjacent tissues during movement.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000077 \"FMA:66773\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000077 \"mesotheliocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26106328\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000077 \"Mesothelial cells, which morphologically resemble squamous epithelial cells, express both epithelial markers (cytokeratins) and mesenchymal markers (vimentin), reflecting their mesodermal origin. They feature surface microvilli and apical-basal polarity. Under certain conditions, they can undergo mesothelial-to-mesenchymal transition. These cells also produce extracellular matrix proteins, maintain serosal homeostasis, and facilitate fluid transport.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Epithelium\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1016/B978-0-12-410424-2.00003-2\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.biologyonline.com/dictionary/stratified-epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000079 \"An epithelial cell, organized into multiple layers, with only the basal layer being in contact with the basement membrane.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000080 \"A cell which moves among different tissues of the body, via blood, lymph, or other medium.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000081 \"A cell found predominately in the blood.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000081 \"FMA:62844\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000081 \"MESH:D001773\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000081 obo:CL_0000988)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000082 \"An epithelial cell of the lung.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000082 \"BTO:0004299\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000082 \"lung epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000083 \"An epithelial cell of the pancreas.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000083 \"BTO:0000028\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000083 \"pancreas epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000083 \"pancreatic epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000084 \"A type of lymphocyte whose defining characteristic is the expression of a T cell receptor complex.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000084 \"BTO:0000782\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000084 \"CALOHA:TS-1001\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000084 \"FMA:62870\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000084 \"MESH:D013601\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000084 \"VHOG:0001479\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000084 \"T lymphocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000084 \"T-cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000084 \"T-lymphocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000084 \"immature T cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000084 \"mature T cell\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000084 obo:CL_0000542)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D007728\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15771589\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17105582\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000091 \"A tissue-resident macrophage of the reticuloendothelial system found on the luminal surface of the hepatic sinusoids involved in erythrocyte clearance. Markers include F4/80+, CD11b-low, CD68-positive, sialoadhesin-positive, CD163/SRCR-positive. Irregular, with long processes including lamellipodia extending into the sinusoid lumen, have flattened nucleus with cytoplasm containing characteristic invaginations of the plasma membrane (vermiform bodies); lie within the sinusoid lumen attached to the endothelial surface; derived from the bone marrow, form a major part of the body's mononuclear phagocyte system.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000091 \"BTO:0000685\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000091 \"FMA:14656\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000091 \"hepatic macrophage\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000091 \"littoral cell of hepatic sinusoid\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000091 \"liver macrophage\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000091 \"macrophagocytus stellatus\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000091 \"stellate cell of von Kupffer\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000091 \"von Kupffer cell\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000091 obo:CL_0000864)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10428500\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15055519\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17380158\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000092 \"A specialized phagocytic cell associated with the absorption and removal of the mineralized matrix of bone tissue, which typically differentiates from monocytes. This cell has the following markers: tartrate-resistant acid phosphatase type 5-positive, PU.1-positive, c-fos-positive, nuclear factor NF-kappa-B p100 subunit-positive, tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 11A-positive and macrophage colony-stimulating factor 1 receptor-positive.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000092 \"BTO:0000968\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000092 \"CALOHA:TS-0721\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000092 \"FMA:66781\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000092 \"MESH:D010010\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000092 \"chondroclast\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000092 obo:CL_0000766)\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000092 obo:CL_0001035)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D006098\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granulocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000094 \"A leukocyte with abundant granules in the cytoplasm.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000094 \"BTO:0000539\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000094 \"BTO:0001026\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000094 \"CALOHA:TS-0422\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000094 \"FMA:62854\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000094 \"granular leucocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000094 \"granular leukocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000094 \"polymorphonuclear leukocyte\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000094 obo:CL_0000766)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009504\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11138776\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12560239\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15514007\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7880385\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000096 \"A fully differentiated neutrophil, a granular leukocyte having a nucleus with three to five lobes connected by slender threads, and cytoplasm containing fine inconspicuous granules and stainable by neutral dyes. They are produced in bone marrow at a rate of 5e10-10e10/day and have a half-life of 6-8 hours. Neutrophils are CD15-positive, CD16-positive, CD32-positive, CD43-positive, CD181-positive, and CD182-positive.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000096 \"poly\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000096 \"polymorphonuclear leucocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000096 \"polymorphonuclear leukocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000096 \"BTO:0003473\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000096 \"PMN\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000096 \"mature neutrocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000096 \"mature neutrophil leucocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000096 \"mature neutrophil leukocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000096 \"mature neutrophilic leucocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000096 \"mature neutrophilic leukocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000096 \"polymorphonuclear neutrophil\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000096 \"polynuclear neutrophilic leucocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000096 \"polynuclear neutrophilic leukocyte\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000096 obo:CL_0000775)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:068340007X\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D008407\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC1312421\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2855166\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15153310\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16455980\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19671378\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:212366338\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9354811\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000097 \"A cell that is found in almost all tissues containing numerous basophilic granules and capable of releasing large amounts of histamine and heparin upon activation. Progenitors leave bone marrow and mature in connective and mucosal tissue. Mature mast cells are found in all tissues, except the bloodstream. Their phenotype is CD117-high, CD123-negative, CD193-positive, CD200R3-positive, and FceRI-high. Stem-cell factor (KIT-ligand; SCF) is the main controlling signal of their survival and development.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000097 \"BTO:0000830\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000097 \"CALOHA:TS-0603\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000097 \"FMA:66784\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000097 \"histaminocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000097 \"labrocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000097 \"mastocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:068340007X\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000097 \"tissue basophil\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000097 obo:CL_0000766)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000098 \"A specialized epithelial cell involved in sensory perception. Restricted to special sense organs of the olfactory, gustatory, and vestibulocochlear receptor systems; contain sensory cells surrounded by supportive, non-receptive cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000098 \"neuroepithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000098 \"BTO:0004301\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D007395\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000099 \"Most generally any neuron which is not motor or sensory. Interneurons may also refer to neurons whose axons remain within a particular brain region as contrasted with projection neurons which have axons projecting to other brain regions.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000099 \"BTO:0003811\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000099 \"FMA:67313\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000099 \"WBbt:0005113\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000099 \"CNS interneuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009046\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16875686\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000100 \"An efferent neuron that passes from the central nervous system or a ganglion toward or to a muscle and conducts an impulse that causes or inhibits movement.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000100 \"BTO:0000312\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000100 \"FMA:83617\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000100 \"WBbt:0005409\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000100 \"motoneuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000101 \"Any neuron having a sensory function; an afferent neuron conveying sensory impulses.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000101 \"BTO:0001037\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000101 \"FMA:84649\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000101 \"MESH:D011984\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000101 \"WBbt:0005759\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23749412\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36381588\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000102 \"A neuron type that respond to multiple stimuli such as mechanical, thermal and chemical. This neuron type is responsible for integrating different types of sensory inputs, allowing organisms to respond appropriately to diverse environmental challenges.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23749412\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000102 \"polymodal sensory neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0444009442\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000103 \"A type of interneuron that has two neurites, usually an axon and a dendrite, extending from opposite poles of an ovoid cell body.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000103 \"FMA:67282\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_0000103 cl:BDS_subset)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FMA:67287\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000104 \"A neuron with three or more neurites, usually an axon and multiple dendrites.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000104 \"FMA:67287\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_0000104 cl:BDS_subset)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FMA:67305\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000105 \"Neuron with two neurites that are fused grossly when they protrude from the soma and bifurcate a short distance from the soma.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000105 \"FMA:67305\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FMA:67278\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:nv\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000106 \"Neuron with one neurite that extends from the cell body.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000106 \"FMA:67278\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_0000106 cl:BDS_subset)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000107 \"A neuron whose cell body is within an autonomic ganglion.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000107 \"FMA:80121\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000108 \"A neuron that uses acetylcholine as a vesicular neurotransmitter.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000108 \"BTO:0004902\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000108 \"FMA:84796\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000108 \"MESH:D059329\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000108 \"WBbt:0006840\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000109 \"MESH:D059331\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23040809\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/B978-012589762-4/50021-9\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000110 \"A neuron that uses neuropeptides as transmitters.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000111 \"OBSOLETE A neuron that is part of nerve found outside the central nervous system.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000111 \"FMA:84664\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34696823\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37608556\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000112 \"A neuron of the invertebrate central nervous system. This neuron innervates the central complex (CX) of an invertebrate brain and it forms columnar patterns with its dendrites. It is involved in navigation and spatial processing.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18837039\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32374034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34696823\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37608556\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9153131\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000112 \"Columnar neurons have been widely studied in Diptera, locusts, honey bees and other insects. In the mammalian brain, a \\\"columnar organisation\\\" is referred to neurons of the neocortex, however these differ from columnar neurons which are found in the insects central nervous system.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000113 \"A vertebrate phagocyte with a single nucleus.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000113 \"BTO:0001433\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000113 obo:CL_0000518)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7892198\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Surface_ectoderm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1101/2024.07.02.601324\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000114 \"An ectodermal cell that is part of the external ectoderm, forming the outermost layer of the developing embryo. It is characterized by its polarized nature, with distinct apical and basal surfaces (Ferrante Jr., Reinke, & Stanley, 1995). Surface ectodermal cell gives rise to the epidermis, hair follicles, nails, sensory organs, and specialized structures like the apical ectodermal ridge crucial for limb development (Skoufa et al., 2024).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000114 \"FMA:72552\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000114 \"cell of surface ectoderm\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1101/2024.07.02.601324\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000114 \"surface ectoderm cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D042783\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21275341\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Endothelial_cell\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://sourceforge.net/tracker/?func=detail&atid=440764&aid=3364936&group_id=36855\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000115 \"An endothelial cell comprises the outermost layer or lining of anatomical structures and can be squamous or cuboidal. In mammals, endothelial cell has vimentin filaments and is derived from the mesoderm.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000115 \"BTO:0001176\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000115 \"CALOHA:TS-0278\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000115 \"FMA:66772\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000115 \"endotheliocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:cvs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000116 \"Pioneer neurons establish a pathway in the developing central nervous system and then undergo programmed cell death once the adult axons, which follow them, have made connections with the target site. Thus, they are a transient cell type involved in axon guidance.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Basket_cell&oldid=951703880\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000118 \"Basket cells are inhibitory GABAergic interneurons of the brain. In general, dendrites of basket cells are free branching and contain smooth spines. Axons are highly branched. The branched axonal arborizations give rise to basket-like structures that surround the soma of the target cell. Basket cells form axo-somatic synapses, meaning their synapses target somas of other cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_0000118 cl:BDS_subset)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"NIFSTD:sao1415726815\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000119 \"Large intrinsic neuron located in the granule layer of the cerebellar cortex that extends its dendrites into the molecular layer where they receive contact from parallel fibers. The axon of the Golgi cell ramifies densely in the granule layer and enters into a complex arrangement with mossy fiber terminals and granule cell dendrites to form the cerebellar glomerulus. Llinas, Walton and Lang. In The Synaptic Organization of the Brain. 5th ed. 2004.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000119 \"MESH:D000080906\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000119 \"Golgi cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000119 \"Golgi neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000119 \"cerebellar Golgi neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000119 \"cerebellum Golgi cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/j.cnp.2022.11.002\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0000119 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/CB_circuits_PMID3650468_f2.png>)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.3389/fnins.2020.00293\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0000119 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Candelabrum_cell.png>)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/granule+cell>) obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000120 \"A neuron of the vertebrate central nervous system that is small in size. This general class includes small neurons in the granular layer of the cerebellar cortex, cerebral cortex neurons that are not pyramidal cells and small neurons without axons found in the olfactory bulb.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000120 \"BTO:0003393\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D011689\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12907269\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14568361\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31424738\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33288911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38168772\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000121 \"An inhibitory neuron and the sole output neuron of the cerebellar cortex, the Purkinje cell's soma is located between the granular and molecular layers of the cerebellum. It is one of the largest neural cells in the mammalian brain, ranging from 50 to 80 micrometres in diameter. Purkinje cells have planar, fan-shaped dendrites that branch extensively with little overlap. This cell type receives synaptic input from parallel fibres, which modulate high-frequency spike activity known as \\\"simple spikes,\\\" and climbing fibres, which modulate infrequent calcium spike activity known as \\\"complex spikes\\\". Purkinje cells are involved in motor coordination, particularly in correcting movements in progress.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000121 \"BTO:0001011\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000121 \"CALOHA:TS-0845\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000121 \"FMA:67969\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28821816\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000121 \"Purkinje neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.proghi.2004.07.002\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000121 \"cerebellar Purkinje cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38168772\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000121 \"PC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28821816\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000121 \"PN\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17535929\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27215193\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37426070\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.stem.2023.11.013\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000121 \"Neurodegenerative disorders affecting Purkinje cells disrupt motor functions. Some of the neurodegenerative disorders that causes loss and degeration of Purkinje cells are Spinocerebellar ataxias (SCAs) (Josef P Kapfhammer and Etsuko Shimobayashi 2023), Friedreich's ataxia (FRDA) (Kevin C Kemp et al., 2016), Fetal alcohol syndrome (Laurent Servais et al., 2016), Dandy-Walker malformation (Alexander Atamian et al., 2024).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/j.cnp.2022.11.002\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0000121 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/CB_circuits_PMID3650468_f2.png>)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.3389/fnins.2020.00293\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0000121 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Candelabrum_cell.jpg>)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:9780123973481\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000122 \"A neuron that has dendritic processes radiating from the cell body forming a star-like shape.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000122 \"BTO:0002316\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_0000122 cl:BDS_subset)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009457\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000125 \"A non-neuronal cell of the nervous system. They not only provide physical support, but also respond to injury, regulate the ionic and chemical composition of the extracellular milieu. Guide neuronal migration during development, and exchange metabolites with neurons.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000125 \"BTO:0002606\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000125 \"CALOHA:TS-0415\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000125 \"FMA:54536\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000125 \"neuroglial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000125 \"neuroglia\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000126 \"A neuroglial cell of ectodermal origin, i.e., the astrocytes and oligodendrocytes considered together.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000126 \"BTO:0000771\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000126 \"CALOHA:TS-2027\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000126 \"FMA:54538\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000126 \"macrogliocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1152/physrev.2001.81.2.871\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003004) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000126 \"macroglia\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D001253\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11746784\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12162730\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12898703\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20942978\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astrocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000127 \"A class of large neuroglial (macroglial) cells in the central nervous system - the largest and most numerous neuroglial cells in the brain and spinal cord. Astrocytes (from 'star' cells) are irregularly shaped with many long processes, including those with 'end feet' which form the glial (limiting) membrane and directly and indirectly contribute to the blood-brain barrier. They regulate the extracellular ionic and chemical environment, and 'reactive astrocytes' (along with microglia) respond to injury.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000127 \"BTO:0000099\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000127 \"CALOHA:TS-0060\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000127 \"FMA:54537\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000127 \"astrocytic glia\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009836\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oligodendrocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000128 \"A class of large neuroglial (macroglial) cells in the central nervous system. Form the insulating myelin sheath of axons in the central nervous system.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000128 \"BTO:0000962\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000128 \"CALOHA:TS-0709\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000128 \"FMA:54540\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:8734446\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000128 \"OLs\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000128 \"oligodendroglia\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000128 obo:CL_0000126)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D017628\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11517395\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12430718\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14561199\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14612429\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16177057\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19461673\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2089275\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microglia\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000129 \"A transcriptomically distinct central nervous system macrophage found in the parenchyma of the central nervous system. Marker include CD11b-positive, F4/80-positive, and CD68-positive.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000129 \"brain macrophage\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000129 \"BTO:0000078\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000129 \"BTO:0000962\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000129 \"FMA:54539\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000129 \"brain-resident macrophage\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de/\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000129 \"hortega cells\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de/\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000129 \"microgliocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000129 \"MF.microglia.CNS\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41598-020-66092-9\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003004) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000129 \"microglia\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23616747\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000129 \"Unlike macroglial cells, microglial cells  arise from hematopoietic stem cells in the yolk sac during early embryogenesis that populate the central nervous system. They derive from embryonic mesoderm and are not from neuroectoderm where glioblast develops from. Markers: Mouse: CD11b+, F4/80+, CD68+. They represent ~12% of the cells in the CNS, but they are not uniformly distributed within the CNS. A normal adult mouse brain has approximately 3.5x10e6 microglia. Microglia are also reportedly CD3-negative, CD4-positive, CD8-negative, CD11b-positive, CD11c-high, CD14-negative, CD19-negative, CD45-low, CD56-negative, CD163-negative, CD200R-positive, CD281-positive, CD282-positive, CD283-positive, CD284-positive, CD285-positive, CD286-positive, CD287-positive, CD288-positive, CD289-positive, Gr1-negative, nestin-positive, and PU.1-positive.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26564856\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000131 \"An endothelial cell that lines the blood and lymphatic vessels of the digestive tract. This cell forms the gut–vascular barrier (GVB) through tight junctions and crosstalk with pericytes and enteric glial cells, regulating the passage of nutrients and immune cells while restricting microbial translocation into the bloodstream.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21976958\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23284695\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34741068\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36769303\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000132 \"An hexagonal, flattened, mitochondria-rich endothelial cell that forms a monolayer on the posterior surface of the cornea (the corneal endothelium). Corneal endothelial cells are derived from the neural crest and are responsible for keeping the cornea transparent by maintaining the tissue in a semi-dry state through the action of their ionic pumps and tight junction barrier.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000132 \"CALOHA:TS-0172\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000132 \"FMA:70614\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:068340007X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000133 \"Ectoderm destined to be nervous tissue.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000133 \"neurectoderm cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FB:ma\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2613570\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10102814\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16923606\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17986482\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19960544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesenchymal_stem_cell\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de/cope.cgi?key=mesenchymal%20stem%20cells\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000134 \"A connective tissue cell that normally gives rise to other cells that are organized as three-dimensional masses. In humans, this cell type is CD73-positive, CD90-positive, CD105-positive, CD45-negative, CD34-negative, and MHCII-negative. They may further differentiate into osteoblasts, adipocytes, myocytes, neurons, or chondroblasts in vitro. Originally described as residing in the bone marrow, this cell type is now known to reside in many, if not all, adult organs.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000134 \"BTO:0002625\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000134 \"BTO:0003298\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000134 \"FMA:70546\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_0000134 \"bone marrow stromal cells\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_0000134 \"colony-forming unit-fibroblast\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11378515\") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_0000134 \"marrow stromal cells\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000134 \"BMSC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000134 \"CFU-F\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11378515\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000134 \"MSC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000134 \"mesenchymal precursor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D044982\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003004) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000134 \"mesenchymal progenitor cells\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000134 \"mesenchymal stem cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000134 \"mesenchymal stromal cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003004) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000134 \"mesenchymal stromal cells\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D044982\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003004) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000134 \"stem cells, mesenchymal\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000134 obo:CL_0002320)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20303382\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20305780\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29286323\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31473260\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32084275\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9177213\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1186/1755-1536-5-S1-S6\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000135 \"A bone marrow-derived cell that predominantly develops from myeloid lineage-restricted progenitor cells and circulates in peripheral blood, characterized by co-expression of hematopoietic markers CD45 and CD34 along with stromal markers including collagen type I in both humans and mice (Chesney et al., 1997; Blakaj and Bucala, 2012). This spindle-shaped cell exhibits a unique dual identity, functionally bridging immune and stromal compartments with characteristics of both monocytes and fibroblasts. Predominantly arising from circulating monocytes, it migrates to injury sites via chemokine receptors and participates in wound repair through extracellular matrix deposition, cytokine secretion, and antigen presentation via MHC class II. As mesenchymal progenitors, fibrocytes can differentiate into fibroblasts, myofibroblasts, and adipocytes, contributing to both physiological repair and pathological fibrosis (Blakaj and Bucala, 2012).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000135 \"FMA:63879\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30826294\") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_0000135 \"monocyte-derived fibrocyte\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000135 obo:CL_0000499)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D017667\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000136 \"A fat-storing cell found mostly in the abdominal cavity and subcutaneous tissue of mammals. Fat is usually stored in the form of triglycerides.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000136 \"BTO:0000443\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000136 \"CALOHA:TS-0012\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000136 \"FMA:63880\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000136 \"adipose cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000136 \"fat cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D010011\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000137 \"A mature osteoblast that has become embedded in the bone matrix. They occupy a small cavity, called lacuna, in the matrix and are connected to adjacent osteocytes via protoplasmic projections called canaliculi.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000137 \"bone cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000137 \"BTO:0002038\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000137 \"CALOHA:TS-1167\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000137 \"FMA:66779\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000137 \"VSAO:0000124\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D019902\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32491508\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000138 \"A skeletogenic cell that secretes a specialized, avascular, GAG-rich matrix, is embedded in cartilage tissue matrix, retains the ability to divide, and develops from a chondroblast cell.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000138 \"BTO:0000249\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000138 \"CALOHA:TS-0138\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000138 \"FMA:66782\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000138 \"cartilage cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000140 \"Skeletogenic cell that secretes dentine matrix, is derived from odontogenic papilla. Embedded in dentine tissue, and is the transformation of a non-terminally differentiated odontoblast cell.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781733901\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000141 \"An osteocytelike cell with numerous processes, trapped in a lacuna in the cement of the tooth.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000141 \"FMA:63003\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19073178\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000142 \"A cell occurring in the peripheral part of the vitreous body of the eye that may be responsible for production of hyaluronic acid and collagen.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000142 \"BTO:0004271\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000142 \"FMA:70620\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000142 \"vitreous cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FB:ma\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000144 \"OBSOLETE: A classification of cells by their primary end goal or behavior.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:consider obo:CL_0000144 \"CL:0000000\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:consider obo:CL_0000144 \"CL:0000003\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:consider obo:CL_0000144 \"CL:0001034\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000145 \"A cell capable of processing and presenting lipid and protein antigens to T cells in order to initiate an immune response.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000145 \"APC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000147 \"A pigment cell is a cell that contains pigment granules.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000147 \"VHOG:0001678\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000147 \"chromatocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000147 \"chromatophore\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000148 \"A pigment cell derived from the neural crest. Contains melanin-filled pigment granules, which gives a brown to black appearance.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000148 \"BTO:0000847\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000148 \"CALOHA:TS-0613\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000148 \"FMA:70545\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000148 \"MESH:D008544\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000148 \"VHOG:0001679\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_0000148 \"melanophore\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000149 \"pigment cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ORCID:0000-0002-7073-9172\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000150 \"An epithelial cell, located in a gland, that is specialised for the synthesis and secretion of specific biomolecules, such as hormones, or mucous.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000150 \"CALOHA:TS-2085\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000150 \"FMA:86494\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000150 \"glandular epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000151 \"A cell that specializes in controlled release of one or more substances.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000151 \"BTO:0003659\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000151 \"FMA:86916\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0198547684\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000152 \"A cell of an exocrine gland; i.e. a gland that discharges its secretion via a duct.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000152 \"FMA:16014\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000153 \"A cell that secretes glycosaminoglycans.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000153 \"GAG secreting cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_0000153 \"hyaluronic acid secreting cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21907708\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30571046\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Gastric_chief_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000155 \"An epithelial cell of the stomach that is part of the fundic gastric gland. This cell is characterized by a basally located nucleus, abundant rough endoplasmic reticulum, and large apical secretory granules. It produces and secretes pepsinogen, the inactive precursor of the digestive enzyme pepsin.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000155 \"FMA:62902\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000155 \"chief cell of stomach\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Chief_cell\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000155 \"gastric chief cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000155 \"pepsinogen secreting cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Chief_cell\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000155 \"zymogenic cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000157 \"A cell that specializes in secretion of surfactant in the alveoli of the lung.\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000157 obo:CL_0000151)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1183/09031936.00146609\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1378/chest.12-2762\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28128362\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29874100\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7905712\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000158 \"A non-mucous, epithelial secretory cell that is part of the tracheobronchial tree. A club cell has short microvilli but no cilia. A club cell is able to multiply and differentiate into ciliated cells to regenerate the bronchiolar epithelium and it also protects the tracheobronchial epithelium.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000158 \"BTO:0004811\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000158 \"FMA:14119\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000158 \"Clara cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D020397\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goblet_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000160 \"A specialized, columnar, mucus secreting epithelial cell shaped like a flask or goblet. A narrow basal end contains the nucleus while the apical end is swollen by the accumulation of mucus laden secretory granules.  Short microvilli project from the apical plasma membrane.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000160 \"BTO:0001540\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000160 \"FMA:13148\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000160 \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goblet_cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000160 \"chalice cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <http://cnx.org/content/col11496/1.6/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=30131227>) foaf:depiction obo:CL_0000160 \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/404_Goblet_Cell_new.jpg/800px-404_Goblet_Cell_new.jpg\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:consider obo:CL_0000161 obo:CL_0000162)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31613538\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31670611\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000162 \"An epithelial cell of the stomach that is part of the fundic gastric gland. This cell is characterized by its pyramidal shape, abundant mitochondria, and a complex network of secretory canaliculi lined with microvilli. It secretes hydrochloric acid into the stomach lumen and produces intrinsic factor, essential for vitamin B12 absorption.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000162 \"BTO:0001780\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000162 \"FMA:62901\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29263912\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000162 \"gastric parietal cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Parietal_cell\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000162 \"oxyntic cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29263912\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31613538\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000162 \"Parietal cells have dynamic, actin-supported microvilli that increase in number during active secretion, playing a crucial role in secreting hydrochloric acid and intrinsic factor. The structure and regulation of these microvilli are influenced by proteins such as ASAP3, which modulates Arf6 activity and actin assembly, thereby controlling microvilli formation and parietal cell function.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D055098\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000163 \"A cell of an endocrine gland, ductless glands that secrete substances which are released directly into the circulation and which influence metabolism and other body functions.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000163 \"FMA:83809\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000163 \"endocrinocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000164 \"An endocrine cell that is located in the epithelium of the gastrointestinal tract or in the pancreas.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000164 \"BTO:0003865\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000164 \"FMA:62930\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000164 \"MESH:D019858\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D055099\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000165 \"A neuron that is capable of some hormone secretion in response to neuronal signals.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000165 \"BTO:0002691\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000165 \"FMA:83810\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000165 \"neurosecretory cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000165 \"neurosecretory neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:5342440\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.clinicalkey.com/#!/content/book/3-s2.0-B9780323555968000073\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000165 \"The neurosecretory cell is neither an ordinary neuron nor an endocrine cell, but a combination of both. Its neuronal features resemble those of ordinary neurons concerning both structure and function. The production of a visible secretory material marks the neurosecretory neuron as a gland cell, and the fact that extractable cellular products act in the manner of hormones places it in the realm of endocrine elements. \nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D019439\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000166 \"A cell that stores epinephrine secretory vesicles. During times of stress, the nervous system signals the vesicles to secrete their hormonal content. Their name derives from their ability to stain a brownish color with chromic salts. Characteristically, they are located in the adrenal medulla and paraganglia of the sympathetic nervous system.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000166 \"BTO:0000259\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000166 \"FMA:69263\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000166 \"phaeochromocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000168 \"BTO:0000783\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pancreatic_b_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000169 \"A cell that secretes insulin and is located towards the center of the islets of Langerhans.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ZFA:0009102\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000169 \"beta cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000169 \"BTO:0000783\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000169 \"EV:0200009\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000169 \"FMA:70586\")\nAnnotation