EBchecked/topic/156177/Deiters-cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000635 \"The outer phalangeal cells of the organ of Corti. This cell holds the base of the hair cell in a cup-shaped depression.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000635 \"FMA:75725\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000635 \"Deiters cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000635 \"outer phalangeal cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:NV\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21911394\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000636 \"Astrocyte-like radial glial cell that extends vertically throughout the retina, with the nucleus are usually in the middle of the inner nuclear layer.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000636 \"BTO:0003064\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.21769/BioProtoc.4179\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType core:MISSPELLING) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000636 \"Muller cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000636 \"Muller glia\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000636 \"Müller cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0618947256\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000637 \"A cell that stains readily in the anterior pituitary gland.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000637 \"FMA:83089\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000638 \"An acidophilic chromophil cell that of the anterior pituitary gland.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000638 \"FMA:83093\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000638 \"acidophil cell of pars anterior of adenohypophysis\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000638 \"acidophil of pars anterior of adenohypophysis\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000638 \"acidophil of pars distalis of adenohypophysis\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000638 \"pituitary alpha cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000639 \"A basophilic chromophil cell that of the anterior pituitary gland.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000639 \"FMA:83094\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000639 \"basophil cell of anterior lobe of hypophysis\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000639 \"beta cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000639 \"pituitary beta cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000641 \"A cell that is resistant to stains.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000641 \"FMA:83626\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000641 \"chromophobic cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10495875\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15961560\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.23937/2572-407X.1510006\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000642 \"An agranular supporting cell of the anterior pituitary (adenohypophysis) that is characterized by a star-like morphology and ability to form follicles. Folliculostellate cells communicate with each other and with endocrine cells via gap junctions.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.23937/2572-407X.1510006\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000642 \"folliculo-stellate cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34734454\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000642 \"pituitary folliculostellate cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34734454\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000642 \"FS cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.23937/2572-407X.1510006\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000642 \"FSC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34734454\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000642 \"Sox2-positive stem cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18287078\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31620083\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34734454\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.23937/2572-407X.1510006\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000642 \"Folliculostellate cells are a heterogeneous group of cells rather than a single cell type, with different morphology and gene expression profiles. Due to this heterogeneity, it is unclear if different properties that have been attributed to folliculostellate cells (pluripotent, proliferative, phagocytic) are common in all folliculostellate cells or limited to particular subsets.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.neurolex.org/wiki/Category:Bergmann_Glial_Cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000644 \"Type of radial astrocyte in the cerebellar cortex that have their cell bodies in the Purkinje cell layer and processes that extend into the molecular layer, terminating with bulbous endfeet at the pial surface. Bergmann glia express high densities of glutamate transporters that limit diffusion of the neurotransmitter glutamate during its release from synaptic terminals. Besides their role in early development of the cerebellum, Bergmann glia are also required for the pruning or addition of synapses.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000644 \"FMA:54559\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000644 \"Bergmann astrocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000644 \"Bergmann glial cell of cerebellum\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.3389/fnins.2020.00293\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_0000644 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Candelabrum_cell.jpg>)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0412046911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31915267\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pituicyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000645 \"A glial cell of astrocytic lineage with long processes running parallel to adjacent axons in the proximal infundibulum of the neurohypophysis. These processes form a three-dimensional network among the axons of the hypothalamic neurosecretory cells and are connected by gap junctions which provide for their metabolic coupling. This cell type constitutes most of the nonexcitable tissue in the neurohypophsis; function may include possibly acting as an intermediate in the modulation of oxytocin and vasopressin release. This cell type is highly variable in size and shape and commonly contain lipid droplets and deposits of lipochrome pigment.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000645 \"BTO:0003793\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000645 \"FMA:83503\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000646 \"Undifferentiated; mitotic stem cell for other epithelial cell types; rounded or elliptical with little cytoplasm and few organelles; contain cytokeratin intermediate filament.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000646 \"BTO:0000939\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000646 \"FMA:62516\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0702022918\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0702024783\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33348900\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Giant_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000647 \"A phagocytic syncytial cell formed by the fusion of macrophages, occurs in chronic inflammatory responses to persistent microorganism such as M.tuberculosis, component of granulomas. Sometimes used to refer to megakaryocytes.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000647 \"BTO:0003107\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000647 \"FMA:83035\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000647 \"MESH:D015726\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0702022918\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0702024783\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000647 \"Langerhans giant cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0702022918\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0702024783\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000647 \"foreign body giant cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0702022918\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0702024783\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000647 \"macrophage polykaryon\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0702022918\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0702024783\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000647 \"multinucleate giant cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0702022918\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0702024783\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000647 \"syncytial giant cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33348900\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000647 \"MGC\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000647 obo:CL_0000766)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:cvs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11457727\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000648 \"A smooth muscle cell that synthesizes, stores, and secretes the enzyme renin. This cell type are located in the wall of the afferent arteriole at the entrance to the glomerulus. While having a different origin than other kidney smooth muscle cells, this cell type expresses smooth muscle actin upon maturation.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000648 \"juxtaglomerular cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000648 \"FMA:84138\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000648 \"JG cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000648 \"renin secreting cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0815332181\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21860392\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32097634\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WIKIPEDIA:Spinous_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000649 \"A keratinocyte found within the stratum spinosum (prickle cell layer) of the epidermis, distinguished by numerous intercellular desmosomes, which give it a “prickly” or spiny appearance. Positioned above the mitotically active basal layer and beneath the granular layer, it contributes to the skin’s mechanical strength and barrier function, preventing water loss and pathogen entry. This cell expresses differentiation-specific keratins K1 and K10 in mice, unlike basal cells that express K5 and K14, and lacks the keratohyalin granules found in granular cells, marking its intermediate stage of epidermal differentiation.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000649 \"FMA:69059\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WIKIPEDIA:Spinous_cell\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000649 \"prickle cell of epidermis\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32843640\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000649 \"spinous keratinocytes of epidermis\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de/cope.cgi?key=mesangial%20cells\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000650 \"A cell type that encapsulates the capillaries and venules in the kidney. This cell secretes mesangial matrix that provides the structural support for the capillaries.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000650 \"BTO:0000853\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000650 \"CALOHA:TS-0617\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000650 \"FMA:70972\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000650 \"MESH:D050527\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000650 \"kidney mesangial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000651 \"OBSOLETE. A mucus-secreting cell, with numerous apical secretory vesicles containing mucins; nucleus are basally displaced; numerous at the neck of mucus secreting glands\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000651 \"neck cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16687276\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinealocyte\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000652 \"This cell type produces and secretes melatonin and forms the pineal parenchyma. Extending from each cell body, which has a spherical, oval or lobulated mucleus, are one or more tortuous basophilic processes, containing parallel microtubules known as synaptic ribbons. These processes end in expanded terminal buds near capillaries or less, frequently, ependymal cells of the pineal recess. The terminal buds contain granular endoplasmic reticulum, mitochondria and electron-dense cored vesicles, which store monoamines and polypeptide hormones, release of which appears to require sympathetic innervation.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000652 \"BTO:0001068\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000652 \"FMA:83417\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1101/2021.10.10.463829\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000653 \"A specialized kidney epithelial cell, contained within a glomerulus, that contains \\\"feet\\\" that interdigitate with the \\\"feet\\\" of other podocytes.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FMA:70967\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000653 \"epithelial cell of visceral layer of glomerular capsule\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000653 \"BTO:0002295\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000653 \"FMA:70967\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FMA:70967\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000653 \"glomerular podocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000653 \"glomerular visceral epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000653 \"kidney podocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000653 \"renal podocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000654 \"A primary oocyte is an oocyte that has not completed female meosis I.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000654 \"BTO:0000512\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000654 \"FMA:18645\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000654 \"primary oogonium\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000654 obo:CL_0000023)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000655 \"A secondary oocyte is an oocyte that has not completed meiosis II.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000655 \"BTO:0003094\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000655 \"FMA:18646\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000655 \"primary oogonium\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000655 obo:CL_0000023)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000656 \"A diploid cell that has derived from a spermatogonium and can subsequently begin meiosis and divide into two haploid secondary spermatocytes.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000656 \"BTO:0001115\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000656 \"CALOHA:TS-2194\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000656 \"FMA:72292\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000657 \"One of the two haploid cells into which a primary spermatocyte divides, and which in turn gives origin to spermatids.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000657 \"BTO:0000709\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000657 \"CALOHA:TS-2195\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000657 \"FMA:72293\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000658 \"An epithelial cell that secretes cuticle.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000659 \"An extracellular matrix secreting cell that secretes eggshell.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000660 \"An extracellular matrix secreting cell that secretes glycocalyx.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1007/978-3-211-99390-3_133\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000666 \"An endothelial cell that has small pores, or fenestrations, which allow for the efficient exchange of substances between the blood and surrounding tissues.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000666 \"window cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000667 \"An extracellular matrix secreting cell that secretes collagen.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000668 \"OBSOLETE: The cell characteristic of an organ, as distinguished from associated connective or supporting tissues.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000668 \"BTO:0002174\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000668 \"FMA:84638\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D020286\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16807374\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17986482\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20024907\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000669 \"An elongated, contractile cell found wrapped about precapillary arterioles outside the basement membrane. Pericytes are present in capillaries where proper adventitia and muscle layer are missing (thus distingushing this cell type from adventitial cells). They are relatively undifferentiated and may become fibroblasts, macrophages, or smooth muscle cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000669 \"BTO:0002441\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000669 \"FMA:63174\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17986482\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000669 \"ARC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000669 \"adventitial reticular cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000669 \"cell of Rouget\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000669 \"pericyte cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000669 \"pericyte of Rouget\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000669 \"adventitial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:1381289\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000670 \"A primordial germ cell is a diploid germ cell precursors that transiently exist in the embryo before they enter into close association with the somatic cells of the gonad and become irreversibly committed as germ cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000670 \"FMA:70567\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000670 \"gonocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000670 \"primitive germ cell\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000670 obo:CL_0000039)\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000670 obo:CL_0000219)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36807509\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000671 \"A follicle cell that migrates from the dorso-anterior part of the oocyte associated follicular epithelium, in between the nurse cells and the oocyte, and participates in the formation of the operculum.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000671 \"centripetal follicle cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000672 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0000290 from Plant Ontology instead. A water conducting cell, tracheid or vessel member.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/S1467-8039(03)00009-4\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000673 \"An intrinsic neuron of the mushroom body of arthropods and annelids. They have tightly packed, cytoplasm-poor cell bodies.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000673 \"mushroom body intrinsic neuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000673 \"globuli cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36531940\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000674 \"A follicle cell that is part of the stalk connecting adjacent egg chambers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000674 \"stalk cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000674 \"stalk follicle cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000675 \"A mature sexual reproductive cell of the female germline.\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000675 obo:CL_0000021)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000676 \"BTO:0001033\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000677 \"Cell of the intestinal epithelium with a brush border made up of many parallel packed microvilli; associated with absorption, particularly of macromolecules.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17560562\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31693445\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000678 \"A neuron with soma location in the central nervous system that project its axon to the contralateral side of a central nervous system. This neuron can have its soma in the spinal cord, in the hemisphere of the brain, in the retina or in the ventral nerve cord of invertebrates.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25960414\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27532244\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31514748\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33438755\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000678 \"Historically, commissural neurons, particularly in the spinal cord, have been used as a model to understand axon guidance during development.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000679 \"WBbt:0006829\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000680 \"A non-terminally differentiated cell that is capable of developing into a muscle cell.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dph\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000681 \"A cell present in the developing CNS. Functions as both a precursor cell and as a scaffold to support neuronal migration.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_0000681 \"forebrain radial glial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:jb\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000682 \"An absorptive cell of the gut epithelium that endocytoses microorganisms and intact macromolecules from the gut lumen and transports them to the subepithelial space where they are presented to antigen-presenting cells and lymphocytes.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000682 \"M cell\"@en)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000682 \"BTO:0003600\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000682 \"FMA:62929\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000682 \"M-cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000682 \"microfold cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://neurolex.org/wiki/Category:Ependymoglial_Cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000683 \"A cell that transports hormones from neurosecretory cells. This nerve cell is characterized by bipolar shape and endfeet that contact a basal lamina around blood vessels, and/or the pia mater or vitreous body of the eye and additionally contact the ventricular surface or sub-retinal space.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000683 \"MESH:D063928\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000683 \"ependymal astrocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PO:0004010\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000685 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0004010 from Plant Ontology instead. A cell synthesizing protoplasm and producing new cells by division and with only a primary cell wall.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000686 \"A columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell that secretes cerebrospinal fluid.\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000686 obo:CL_0000151)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000687 \"R1 cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000688 \"A fibroblast-like cell that provides support at neuromuscular junctions in vertebrates and are localized outside the synaptic basal lamina.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000689 \"A cell with both myofibrils and secretory granules.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000690 \"R2 cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_0000691 cl:BDS_subset)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16136171\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000692 \"A neuroglial cell of the peripheral nervous system inside the basal lamina of the neuromuscular junction providing chemical and physical support to the synapse.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000692 \"Schwann cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18803315\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000692 \"perisynaptic Schwann cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18803315\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000692 \"teloglia\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18803315\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000692 \"tSC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17122314\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000693 \"An interneuron that has spider-like appearance with a small round soma, a large number (7-10) of short, smooth, or slightly beaded primary dendrites that give rise to only a few secondary branches, and a branched axon that establishes a dense axonal mesh with thin shafts.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18568015\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000693 \"NGF cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:3235828\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000693 \"neuroglioform cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000693 \"spiderweb cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:inSubset obo:CL_0000693 cl:BDS_subset)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000694 \"R3 cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10600995\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34047341\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36774666\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37775311\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9728912\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000695 \"A type of transient, early-born glutamatergic neuron located primarily in the marginal zone (future layer I) of the developing cerebral cortex and hippocampus in vertebrates. it is characterized by a bipolar morphology with an elongated soma, a single thick dendrite oriented toward the pial surface, and a long, thin axon that extends tangentially to form horizontal plexuses across the cortical surface. It is important for the multiple developmental processes including migration, dendritogenesis and synaptogenesis. It typically undergoes programmed cell death following cortical maturation with species- and region specific patterns of survival. In mice, it is predominantly observed in the hippocampal formation, particularly in the stratum lacunosum-moleculare and outer molecular layer of the dentate gyrus (van Bruggen et al., 2023). In contrast, in humans, a second morphologically distinct subpopulation emerges mid-gestation and persists postnatally, with surviving cells observed in the cortical sulci and the hippocampus.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Cajal–Retzius_cell&oldid=1032081753\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000695 \"CR cells\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Cajal–Retzius_cell&oldid=1032081753\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000695 \"Horizontal cells of Cajal\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10600995\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000695 \"While previously called 'pioneer neurons' of the marginal zone, Cajal-Retzius cells are differentiated from pioneer neurons (which are Reln-negative) by their Reln-immunoreactivity.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15153415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000696 \"A cell that stores and secretes pancreatic polypeptide hormone.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000696 \"FMA:62938\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000696 \"FMA:83409\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000696 \"type F enteroendocrine cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000697 \"R4 cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000699 \"A type of glomus or chief cell, is sensitive to hypoxia and produce catecholamines.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dhill\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000700 \"A neuron that releases dopamine as a neurotransmitter.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000700 \"BTO:0004032\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000700 \"FMA:84787\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000700 \"MESH:D059290\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000700 \"WBbt:0006746\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000700 \"dopaminergic cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000701 \"Supports paraganglial type 1 cell.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000702 \"R5 cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000703 \"Cell that provides some or all mechanical, nutritional and phagocytic support to their neighbors.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000703 \"BTO:0002315\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15376331\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000704 \"A specialized endothelial cell that senses extracellular signals and guides the directed growth of blood vessels.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000705 \"R6 cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15561411\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9550134\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000706 \"A specialized ependymal cell that is part of the choroid plexus epithelium, responsible for producing cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) by selectively filtering and modifying blood plasma components before secreting it into the brain and spinal cord. This cell is characterized by a brush border on its apical surface, which enhances the secretion of CSF.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1101/2022.10.12.511898\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000706 \"choroid plexus cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000706 \"FMA:70549\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000706 \"epithelial cell of choroid plexus\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25729351\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000706 \"A choroid plexus epithelial cell possesses non-motile 9+0 cilia. While these cilia can exhibit transient motility during development, they generally do not contribute significantly to the directional flow of cerebrospinal fluid (CSF). Instead, they are primarily involved in sensory functions.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000707 \"R7 cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000708 \"Stromal cell that forms the internal covering of the vertebrate brain and produces ECM for this and the choroid plexus.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000708 \"leptomemingeal cell\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000708 obo:CL_0000327)\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000708 obo:CL_0002320)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000709 \"R8 cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000710 \"Epithelial cells derived from neural plate and neural crest.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000710 \"neuroepithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000710 \"BTO:0004301\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000710 \"FMA:70557\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.org/cope.cgi?key=cumulus%20cells\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000711 \"Cumulus cell is a specialized granulosa cell that surrounds and nourishes the oocyte. This cell-type surrounds the fully-grown oocyte to form a cumulus-oocyte complex (abbr. COC). The terms cumulus oophorus cells, cumulus granulosa cells, cumulus oophorous granulosa cells, granulosa-cumulus cells are used to make a distinction between this cell and the other functionally different subpopulation of granulosa cells at the wall of the Graafian follicle.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000711 \"BTO:0002236\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000711 \"MESH:D054885\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000711 \"cumulus cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15582775\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000717 \"OBSOLETE. A subset of motor neurons that innervates intrafusal muscle fibers and has small diameter axons.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34343526\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1017/CBO9780511818202.023\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000718 \"A cell of an ommatidium that secretes lens materials.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000718 \"Semper cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000718 \"cone cell (sensu Endopterygota)\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1242/jcs.s3-105.71.331\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000718 \"Not to be confused with the Semper cells of the Semper organ found in gastropods.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO:0048103\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000723 \"A stem cell that can give rise to cell types of the body other than those of the germ-line.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000723 \"CALOHA:TS-2086\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000723 \"MESH:D053687\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MA:ma\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000724 \"A differentiated cell that functions as a site of nitrogen fixation under aerobic conditions.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000724 \"BTO:0000600\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:085199377X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000726 \"An asexual 1-celled spore (primarily for perennation, not dissemination). Originates endogenously and singly within part of a pre-existing cell by the contraction of the protoplast. Possesses an inner secondary and often thickened hyaline or brown wall, usually impregnated with hydrophobic material.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MA:ma\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000730 \"A cell at the front of a migrating epithelial sheet.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MA:ma\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41385-022-00565-0\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000731 \"A cell of a layer of transitional epithelium in the wall of the proximal urethra, bladder, ureter or renal pelvis, external to the lamina propria.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000731 \"FMA:84127\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_0000731 \"urinary tract transitional epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1242/dev.00702\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000735 \"A hemocyte that derives from the larval lymph gland.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000737 \"Muscle cell which has as its direct parts myofilaments organized into sarcomeres.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000737 \"BTO:0002916\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000737 \"CALOHA:TS-2157\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000737 \"FMA:86936\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:978-0-323-05290-0\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000738 \"An achromatic cell of the myeloid or lymphoid lineages capable of ameboid movement, found in blood or other tissue.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000738 \"BTO:0000751\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000738 \"CALOHA:TS-0549\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000738 \"FMA:62852\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000738 \"MESH:D007962\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000738 \"NCIT:C12529\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40794848\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000738 \"WBC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000738 \"leucocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000738 \"white blood cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000738 \"immune cell\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000738 obo:CL_0000988)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dph\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000740 \"The set of neurons that receives neural inputs via bipolar, horizontal and amacrine cells. The axons of these cells make up the optic nerve.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000740 \"BTO:0001800\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000740 \"FMA:67765\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000740 \"MESH:D012165\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000740 \"gangliocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000740 \"ganglion cell of retina\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41598-020-66092-9\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000740 \"RGC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41598-020-66092-9\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003004) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000740 \"RGCs\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16267219\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000741 \"A motor neuron that is located in the cervical region of the spinal cord and selectively innervates the sternocleidmastoid or trapezius muscle. Unlike other motor neurons, they extend axons dorsally along lateral margins of the spinal cord.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000741 \"SACMN\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15951842\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000742 \"A round chondrocyte that first differentiates in the late embryonic growth plate of bone.\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000742 obo:CL_0000138)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15951842\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25321476\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35179487\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000743 \"A chondrocyte that is part of the hypertrophic cartilage zone. This cell is significantly enlarged and characterised by high expression of type X collagen (COL10A1) in both humans and mice. It actively coordinates endochondral ossification by mineralising the extracellular matrix, attracting blood vessels via angiogenic signalling, and mediating the transition from cartilage to bone - often by transdifferentiating into an osteoblast rather than undergoing apoptosis.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35179487\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000743 \"Despite historical descriptions as 'terminally differentiated,' hypertrophic chondrocytes survive and transdifferentiate into osteoblasts. Genetic lineage tracing shows that hypertrophic chondrocytes do not simply undergo apoptosis but cross the cartilage–bone boundary, dedifferentiate into skeletal stem/progenitor cells, and then redifferentiate into osteoblasts and osteocytes. Single-cell RNA-seq further indicates that these chondrocyte-derived SSPCs are a major source of trabecular osteoblasts and marrow adipocytes.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15951842\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000744 \"A columnar chondrocyte that differentiates in the late embryonic growth plate of bone. Columnar chondrocytes vigorously proliferate and form columns in the growth plate.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0195088433\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000745 \"A neuron that laterally connects other neurons in the inner nuclear layer of the retina.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000745 \"BTO:0004120\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000745 \"horizontal cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41598-020-66092-9\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000745 \"HC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41598-020-66092-9\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003004) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000745 \"HCs\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:mtg_cardiacconduct_nov11\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0323052908\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22426062\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:4711263\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000746 \"Cardiac muscle cells are striated muscle cells that are responsible for heart contraction. In mammals, the contractile fiber resembles those of skeletal muscle but are only one third as large in diameter, are richer in sarcoplasm, and contain centrally located instead of peripheral nuclei.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000746 \"cardiocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000746 \"BTO:0001539\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000746 \"CALOHA:TS-0115\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000746 \"FMA:14067\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000746 \"MESH:D032383\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO:0048739\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000746 \"cardiac muscle fiber\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000746 \"cardiac myocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000746 \"cardiomyocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000746 \"heart muscle cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000747 \"A pigment cell derived from the neural crest. Contains blue pigment of unknown chemical composition in fibrous organelles termed cyanosomes. This gives a blue appearance.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000747 \"blue chromatophore\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000748 \"A bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner plexiform layer.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41598-020-66092-9\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000748 \"BC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41598-020-66092-9\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003004) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000748 \"BCs\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"geo:GSE137537\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003004) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000748 \"BPs\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000749 \"A bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. These cells depolarize in response to light stimulation of their corresponding photoreceptors.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000750 \"A bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with photoreceptors cells and neurons in the outer half of the inner plexiform layer. These cells depolarize in response to light to dark transition.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000751 \"A bipolar neuron found in the retina that is synapsed by rod photoreceptor cells but not by cone photoreceptor cells.  These neurons depolarize in response to light.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38627529\") obo:RO_0002175 obo:CL_0000751 obo:NCBITaxon_32443)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000751 \"FMA:67750\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000752 \"A bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptor cells and neurons in the inner plexiform layer.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000753 \"An OFF-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the outer half of the inner plexiform layer. The cell body of these cells is in the middle of the inner plexiform layer. The dendritic tree is stout and the axon terminates in sublamina 1. The axonal terminal is wide and has only a few varicosities.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000753 \"DB1 cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27565351\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000754 \"An OFF-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the outer half of the inner plexiform layer. The dendritic tree is not well filled and the dendrites are more delicate than in type 1 cells. The axon terminal is bushier and exhibits a dense plexus of varicosities in the inner part of sublamina 1 (Ghosh et al., 2004).  It can be differentiated from other retinal bipolar neurons by its expression of marker genes: Neto1, Lhx3 and Irx-6 (Shekhar, 2016).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000754 \"FMB cone bipolar cell\")\nEquivalentClasses(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27565351\") obo:CL_0000754 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000748 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P50481) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q8R4I7) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q9ER75)))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000755 \"An OFF-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the outer half of the inner plexiform layer. The dendritic tree is delicate and the dendritic tips appear small when compared with type 1 cells. The axon terminal is stratified and restricted to sublamina 2 of the inner plexiform layer.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000755 \"DB2 cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000756 \"An OFF-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the outer half of the inner plexiform layer. The cell has a diffuse axon terminal with varicosities in sublaminae 1 and 2 of the inner plexiform layer.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000756 \"DB3 cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000757 \"An ON-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. The axon terminal is restricted to sublamina 3 of the inner plexiform layer. It is narrowly stratified and branched. The dendritic tree has many delicate branches.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000757 \"DB4 cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000758 \"An ON-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. The cell has a loose, delicate axon terminal that opens in sublamina 3 of the inner plexiform layer and descends into sublamina 4.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000758 \"DB5 cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000759 \"An ON-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. The axon terminal is narrowly stratified and are found just below a calretinin-expressing band in sublamina 4 of the inner plexiform layer.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000759 \"IMB cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000760 \"An ON-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. This cell has the widest dendritic field and the widest axon terminal of all retinal bipolar cells. The axon terminal is delicate and stratified through sublaminae 4 and 5 of the inner plexiform layer.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000760 \"DB6 cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14689473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000761 \"An ON-bipolar neuron found in the retina and having connections with cone photoreceptors cells and neurons in the inner half of the inner plexiform layer. The dendritic tree is wide and the dendritic convergence indicates cone selectivity. The axon terminal is sparsely branched and terminates in sublamina 5 of the inner plexiform layer.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000761 \"BB cone bipolar cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16360205\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000762 \"A nucleated blood cell involved in coagulation, typically seen in birds and other non-mammalian vertebrates.\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000762 obo:CL_0000763)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000763 \"A cell of the monocyte, granulocyte, mast cell, megakaryocyte, or erythroid lineage.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000763 \"BTO:0001441\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000763 \"CALOHA:TS-0647\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000763 \"MESH:D022423\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000763 obo:CL_0000988)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000764 \"A immature or mature cell in the lineage leading to and including erythrocytes.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000764 \"CALOHA:TS-0290\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000764 \"FMA:62845\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000764 \"FMA:83516\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000764 \"erythropoietic cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18174176\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000765 \"A nucleated precursor of an erythrocyte that lacks hematopoietic lineage markers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000765 \"BTO:0001571\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000765 \"CALOHA:TS-0289\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000765 \"FMA:83504\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000765 \"MESH:D004900\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000765 \"normoblast\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000765 obo:CL_0000764)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000766 \"A cell of the monocyte, granulocyte, or mast cell lineage.\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000766 obo:CL_0000738)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D001491\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2626675\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11927641\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19741522\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21236338\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9933081\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000767 \"Any of the immature or mature forms of a granular leukocyte that in its mature form has an irregularly shaped, pale-staining nucleus that is partially constricted into two lobes, and with cytoplasm that contains coarse, bluish-black granules of variable size. Basophils contain vasoactive amines such as histamine and serotonin, which are released on appropriate stimulation. A basophil is CD123-positive, CD193-positive, CD203c-positive, and FceRIa-positive.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000767 \"polymorphonuclear leucocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000767 \"polymorphonuclear leukocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000767 \"BTO:0000129\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000767 \"CALOHA:TS-0073\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000767 \"FMA:62862\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000767 \"basophilic leucocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000767 \"basophilic leukocyte\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000767 obo:CL_0000094)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000768 \"Any of the immature forms of a basophil, in which basophilic specific granules are present but other phenotypic features of the mature form may be lacking.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000768 \"immature basophilic leucocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000768 \"immature basophilic leukocyte\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000768 obo:CL_0000767)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18466030\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000769 \"A basophil precursor in the granulocytic series, being a cell intermediate in development between a basophilic myelocyte and a band form basophil. The nucleus becomes indented where the indentation is smaller than half the distance to the farthest nuclear margin; chromatin becomes coarse and clumped; specific granules predominate while primary granules are rare. Markers are CD11b-positive, CD15-positive, CD16-positive, CD24-positive, CD33-positive, and CD13-positive.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000769 \"FMA:84198\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000769 obo:CL_0000768)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18466030\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000770 \"A late basophilic metamyelocyte in which the nucleus is in the form of a curved or coiled band, not having acquired the typical multilobar shape of the mature basophil.\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000770 obo:CL_0000768)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2626675\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10914487\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:1662676\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000771 \"Any of the immature or mature forms of a granular leukocyte with a nucleus that usually has two lobes connected by one or more slender threads of chromatin, and cytoplasm containing coarse, round granules that are uniform in size and which can be stained by the dye eosin. Eosinophils are CD9-positive, CD191-positive, and CD193-positive.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000771 \"polymorphonuclear leucocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000771 \"polymorphonuclear leukocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000771 \"BTO:0000399\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000771 \"CALOHA:TS-0279\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000771 \"FMA:62861\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000771 \"MESH:D004804\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000771 \"eosinocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000771 \"eosinophilic granulocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000771 \"eosinophilic leucocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000771 \"eosinophilic leukocyte\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000771 obo:CL_0000094)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000772 \"Any of the immature forms of an eosinophil, in which eosinophilic specific granules are present but other phenotypic features of the mature form may be lacking.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000772 \"immature eosinocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000772 \"immature eosinophilic leucocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000772 \"immature eosinophilic leukocyte\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000772 obo:CL_0000771)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19622087\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000773 \"A eosinophil precursor in the granulocytic series, being a cell intermediate in development between a eosinophilic myelocyte and a band form eosinophil. The nucleus becomes indented where the indentation is smaller than half the distance to the farthest nuclear margin; chromatin becomes coarse and clumped; specific gr