s layer; at the base, with expanded end-feet containing numerous lamellated dense bodies resembling lipofuscin of neurons.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000853 \"FMA:62302\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000853 \"olfactory epithelial support cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000853 \"olfactory sustentacular cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000853 \"supporting cell of olfactory epithelium\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000853 \"sustentaculocyte of olfactory epithelium\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000854 \"Interneuromast cell is a neuroectodermal cell deposited by the migrating lateral line primordium between the neuromasts. Interneuromast cells proliferate and migrate to form additional neuromasts.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000855 \"Hair cell is a mechanoreceptor cell that is sensitive to movement of the hair-like projections (stereocilia and kinocilia) which relay the information centrally in the nervous system.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000855 \"hair cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000855 \"BTO:0004744\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000856 \"Neuromast hair cell is a hair cell that acts as a sensory receptor of the neuromast; it is morphologically polarized as a result of the relative position of the single kinocilium and the clusters of stereocilia on its apical surface.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000857 \"A skeletal muscle myoblast that differentiates into slow muscle fibers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000858 \"A skeletal muscle myoblast that differentiates into fa