 mammalian species that the urothelial basal cell type is distinguished by expression of high levels of cytokeratin-5 (CK5), p63 and the signalling molecule Sonic hedgehog (Shh). Similar to intermediate cells, the urothelial basal cell type expresses CK17 but is negative for uroplakins (UPK) and CK20. Urothelial basal cells have also been noted to be smaller in diameter than urothelial intermediate cells.\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_1000486 obo:CL_0000646)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1000487 \"A smooth muscle cell that is part of the prostate gland.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_1000487 \"FMA:84583\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FMA:84583\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_1000487 \"smooth muscle fiber of prostate\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_1000487 obo:CL_0000192)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16550043\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18356246\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1000488 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the bile duct. Cholangiocytes contribute to bile secretion via net release of bicarbonate and water. They are cuboidal epithelium in the small interlobular bile ducts, but become columnar and mucus secreting in larger bile ducts approaching the porta hepatis and the extrahepatic ducts.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_1000488 \"FMA:86481\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_1000488 \"epithelial cell of bile duct\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_1000488 obo:CL_0000069)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1000489 \"A reticular cell that is part of the splenic cord.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_1000489 \"FMA:86497\")\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo